{"_id":"6a2ff42e2204ffbc59e5a542","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"mAOljEWt_0Hb9jLBKuc-H","description":"# Array Operations\n\nNumPy supports a wide range of array operations: element-wise arithmetic, aggregation functions (`sum`, `mean`, `std`, `min`, `max`), reshaping, stacking, and splitting. These operations are vectorized, meaning they apply to the entire array at once without explicit loops, making them highly efficient.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Indexing on ndarrays","url":"https://numpy.org/doc/stable/user/basics.indexing.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb1d"},{"type":"article","title":"NumPy Array Indexing","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/numpy/numpy_array_indexing.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb1e"},{"type":"article","title":"NumPy Array Slicing","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/numpy/numpy_array_slicing.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb1f"},{"type":"article","title":"Indexing Arrays","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/introducing-numpy-part-2-indexing-arrays-5b381b90d1d0/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb20"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:46:38.669Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/mAOljEWt_0Hb9jLBKuc-H.md"}